snp4.14:11.1 starts: Doing jhāna, not footloose,
snp4.14:11.2 starts: he should refrain from restlessness,
snp4.14:11.3 starts: shouldn’t be heedless,
snp4.14:11.4 starts: should live in a noise-less abode.
snp4.14:2.1 starts: “He should put an entire stop
snp4.14:2.3 starts: to the root of objectification-classifications:
snp4.14:2.4 starts: He should train, always mindful,
snp4.14:2.5 starts: to subdue any craving inside him.
snp4.15:8.1 starts: He should conquer drowsiness,
snp4.15:8.2 starts: shouldn’t consort with heedlessness,
snp4.15:8.3 starts: shouldn’t stand firm in his pride—
snp4.15:8.4 starts: the man with his heart set
snp4.15:16.1 starts: For whom, in name-&-form,
snp4.15:16.2 starts: there’s no sense of mine,
snp4.15:16.3 starts: and who doesn’t grieve
snp4.15:16.4 starts: He, in the world,
snp4.15:18.1 starts: Not harsh,
snp4.15:18.2 starts: not perturbed,
snp4.15:18.3 starts: This is the reward
snp4.15:18.4 starts: for those who are free
snp4.16:2.1 starts: as the One with Eyes
snp4.16:2.2 starts: who appears to the world with its devas,
snp4.16:2.3 starts: having dispelled all darkness,
snp4.16:2.4 starts: having arrived at delight
snp4.16:6.1 starts: how many the dangers in the world
snp4.16:6.2 starts: for the monk going the direction
snp4.16:6.3 starts: over which he should prevail
snp4.16:6.4 starts: there in his isolated abode?
snp4.16:9.1 starts: The Buddha:
snp4.16:9.3 starts: what is comfort
snp4.16:9.4 starts: if he’s resorting to a place remote,
snp4.16:9.5 starts: desiring self-awakening
snp4.16:10.1 starts: An enlightened monk,
snp4.16:10.2 starts: shouldn’t fear the five fears:
snp4.16:10.3 starts: of horseflies, mosquitoes, snakes,
snp4.16:10.4 starts: human contact, four-footed beings;
snp4.16:14.1 starts: He shouldn’t come under the sway
snp4.16:14.2 starts: Having dug up their root
snp4.16:14.3 starts: Then, when prevailing
snp4.16:14.4 starts: he’d prevail over notions of dear & undear.
snp4.16:16.1 starts: ‘What will I eat,
snp4.16:16.2 starts: How badly I slept.
snp4.16:16.3 starts: These lamenting thoughts
snp4.16:16.4 starts: one under training,
snp5.1:1.1 starts: Prologue
snp5.1:1.2 starts: a brahman [Bāvarī]
snp5.1:1.3 starts: who had mastered mantras,
snp5.1:1.4 starts: aspiring to nothingness,
